# Line endings, pinned in the repo rather than left to each clone.
#
# The index here is entirely LF today, but only because everyone who has
# committed happened to have `core.autocrlf=true`. A contributor with it off
# would commit CRLF and every later diff would be noise. `text=auto` makes
# that a property of the repository instead of of the machine.
#
# This does NOT silence "LF will be replaced by CRLF": that fires when a file
# in the working copy is LF while the checkout rule says CRLF, and it is
# telling the truth. Set `core.safecrlf=false` locally if the warning is not
# wanted, or `eol=lf` below to keep working copies LF too -- which would
# rewrite the ~146 files currently checked out CRLF.
* text=auto

# Named so their handling does not depend on the content heuristic.
*.zig text
*.zon text
*.md text
*.json text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.gd text
*.tscn text
*.godot text
*.cfg text
*.gdextension text
*.uid text
*.h text

# LF regardless of platform: CRLF breaks the shebang line.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.svg binary
*.ttf binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.exe binary
